                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "41b0a6e5-20ed-3122-adbb-4856e22a3008",
                        "entry_id": "7b05ca5a-05dc-3c34-b180-f67d985837a1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Langue ou dialecte propre à un village ou une vallée."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0bbfe2d1-3db5-4507-87fc-74202484d611",
                                "sense_id": "41b0a6e5-20ed-3122-adbb-4856e22a3008",
                                "text": "Le fait que le vieux fermier de Trifouilly-les-Oies emploie un code ou un répertoire linguistique différent de celui du marchand local, et que ce dernier utilise à son tour une “variété” distincte de celle de l'instituteur à l'école n'est pas dû à des solidarités occultes tracées à l’intérieur des classes sociales , mais tout simplement à la circonstance que la langue du fermier se rapproche davantage du “topolecte” de Trifouilly-les-Oies, […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dbc2d080-fda8-4045-88c2-470234a3c377",
                        "source_entry_id": "7b05ca5a-05dc-3c34-b180-f67d985837a1",
                        "source_sense_id": "41b0a6e5-20ed-3122-adbb-4856e22a3008",
                        "target_lang_word": "topolect",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "topolect",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e460a795-5cf8-37ea-aff3-46f800addbbb",
                                        "entry_id": "3aa0569d-7cc4-3f10-a36f-a2f6e5edfeb5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The speech form, variety (lect) of a particular place or region."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55c1eff2-e9f7-4ed7-aa63-5db96af58a77",
                                                "sense_id": "e460a795-5cf8-37ea-aff3-46f800addbbb",
                                                "text": "We can then establish and name further categories by means of the word \"group\" and the prefix \"sub-\", thus obtaining SUBDIALECT (\"Untermundart\") between topolect and dialect, DIALECT GROUP (\"Mundartengruppe\") between dialect and language, SUBFAMILY (\"Unterfamilie\") between language and family,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6aa3def-ea95-4fc4-a263-1642c3854355",
                                                "sense_id": "e460a795-5cf8-37ea-aff3-46f800addbbb",
                                                "text": "The degree to which Yahudic lects differ from coterritorial non-Jewish lects varies spatially, chronologically, stylistically, and idiolectically (for this reason it is important to study each Yahudic topolect together with its coterritorial Arabic topolect if it has one)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a9b0d627-1956-3e9f-b996-f0348baf1e05",
                                        "entry_id": "3aa0569d-7cc4-3f10-a36f-a2f6e5edfeb5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A regional variety of Chinese; especially a lect other than Standard Mandarin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "325d2c31-90c7-4492-9ebe-c4c0f390f130",
                                                "sense_id": "a9b0d627-1956-3e9f-b996-f0348baf1e05",
                                                "text": "Imminent Chinese linguist Zhou Youguang has said that everyone’s mother tongue is a topolect, whereas China’s standard spoken language has long been the “teacher tongue.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
